# detection_scanner/ttps/_drafts/ — local-only scraper output

This directory is the landing zone for candidate TTP cards emitted by the
`cortex-scraper` (see the `scraper_contract` block in
`../../sources/source-registry.json`). Drafts arrive here with
`status: "draft"` and a `TTP-{YYYY}-{NNNN}-{slug}.json` filename.

Drafts are **local-only and never committed**. A human reviewer promotes a
draft to the active corpus by moving it up to `ttps/` and flipping its status
to `active` *after* it passes `scripts/validate.py` and has been enriched with
Cortex-specific fields (IOCs, BIOCs, product mapping, use cases).

Only this `.gitkeep` is tracked; every `*.json` under `_drafts/` is gitignored
(see the repo-root `.gitignore`). The directory exists so the documented
promote-from-drafts workflow has a stable, committed home.
